y links to videos\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Not tagged as video but contains mostly links to videos","submitter_user":"hugoarnal","user_is_author":false,"tags":["programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/cmrfrj","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/cmrfrj/some_software_talks_i_like"},{"short_id":"lmnmwg","created_at":"2026-08-08T08:43:49.919-05:00","title":"Amiga August 2026 Update","url":"https://amiga.com/news/20260804-amiga-update","score":13,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"orib","user_is_author":false,"tags":["historical","osdev"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/lmnmwg","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/lmnmwg/amiga_august_2026_update"},{"short_id":"dfkuly","created_at":"2026-08-08T07:14:08.620-05:00","title":"Skred (self-created sound engine) as an effects box","url":"","score":-1,"flags":2,"comment_count":0,"description":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://youtu.be/aDWJljOwHuc?si=iQa6RKruoFdKtqKX\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003ehttps://youtu.be/aDWJljOwHuc?si=iQa6RKruoFdKtqKX\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis video shows off a GUI front end experiment to use the Skred sound engine as an audio effect processor.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe \"design\" of the effect is inspired by the digital delay line of the Korg DW-8000, so the parameters directly related to the delay line match that rather than any \"real life\" units.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is all MIT open source code and binaries hosted at github com octetta ddl8k\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eQuestions and comments are really appreciated.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"https://youtu.be/aDWJljOwHuc?si=iQa6RKruoFdKtqKX\r\n\r\nThis video shows off a GUI front end experiment to use the Skred sound engine as an audio effect processor.\r\n\r\nThe \"design\" of the effect is inspired by the digital delay line of the Korg DW-8000, so the parameters directly related to the delay line match that rather than any \"real life\" units.\r\n\r\nThis is all MIT open source code and binaries hosted at github com octetta ddl8k\r\n\r\nQuestions and comments are really appreciated.","submitter_user":"octetta","user_is_author":true,"tags":["c","go","vibecoding"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/dfkuly","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/dfkuly/skred_self_created_sound_engine_as"},{"short_id":"uny1fo","created_at":"2026-08-08T03:57:33.462-05:00","title":"They don’t make ’em like Sublime Text anymore","url":"https://dbushell.com/2026/08/07/sublime-text/","score":77,"flags":0,"comment_count":39,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"diktomat","user_is_author":false,"tags":["editors","rant"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/uny1fo","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/uny1fo/they_don_t_make_em_like_sublime_text"},{"short_id":"ejx00p","created_at":"2026-08-08T01:53:26.705-05:00","title":"Building Groovie, an Advanced Web-Based Drum Machine / Beat Sequencer","url":"https://pointersgonewild.com/2026-08-06-building-groovie-an-advanced-web-based-drum-beat-sequencer/","score":11,"flags":0,"comment_count":1,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"abhin4v","user_is_author":false,"tags":["art","web"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/ejx00p","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/ejx00p/building_groovie_advanced_web_based_drum"},{"short_id":"robrw0","created_at":"2026-08-07T23:45:36.812-05:00","title":"‘Farewell, Etaoin Shrdlu’","url":"https://archive.org/details/FarewellEtaoinShrdlu","score":12,"flags":3,"comment_count":6,"description":"\u003cp\u003ePerhaps does not meet the bar for topicality, but it feels very relevant to the current software zeitgeist.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\"It's inevitable that we're going to go into computers. All the knowledge I've acquired over these 26 years is all locked up in a little box now called a computer. I think most jobs are probably going to end up the same way.\" @13:51\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMore direct source from the New York Times: \u003ca href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/video/insider/100000004687429/farewell-etaoin-shrdlu.html\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003ehttps://www.nytimes.com/video/insider/100000004687429/farewell-etaoin-shrdlu.html\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYouTube mirror for those that prefer it: \u003ca href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1MGjFKs9bnU\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003ehttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1MGjFKs9bnU\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Perhaps does not meet the bar for topicality, but it feels very relevant to the current software zeitgeist.\r\n\r\n\"It's inevitable that we're going to go into computers. All the knowledge I've acquired over these 26 years is all locked up in a little box now called a computer. I think most jobs are probably going to end up the same way.\" @13:51\r\n\r\nMore direct source from the New York Times: https://www.nytimes.com/video/insider/100000004687429/farewell-etaoin-shrdlu.html\r\n\r\nYouTube mirror for those that prefer it: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1MGjFKs9bnU","submitter_user":"lyall","user_is_author":false,"tags":["historical","video"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/robrw0","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/robrw0/farewell_etaoin_shrdlu"},{"short_id":"9cv8me","created_at":"2026-08-07T21:33:45.612-05:00","title":"The Nixpkgs core team has disbanded","url":"https://discourse.nixos.org/t/the-nixpkgs-core-team-has-disbanded/79413","score":91,"flags":2,"comment_count":12,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"kevinc","user_is_author":false,"tags":["nix"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/9cv8me","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/9cv8me/nixpkgs_core_team_has_disbanded"},{"short_id":"ekxllh","created_at":"2026-08-07T19:52:03.302-05:00","title":"BasicSync: A simple app for running Syncthing on Android","url":"https://github.com/chenxiaolong/BasicSync","score":9,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"tffr","user_is_author